# Publish output
[Pp]ublish/
*.[Pp]ublish.xml
*.azurePubxml
*.pubxml
*.publishproj

# Except the native library's, which carry no credentials - only a runtime identifier
# and an output directory. They are the single place the Publish dialog and the
# command line both read, so an ignored one is a setting that exists on one machine
# and nowhere else, and a Publish button that works for whoever wrote it.
# The .user file beside them stays out: that is where anything personal would land.
!bindings/native/Properties/PublishProfiles/*.pubxml
*.pubxml.user

# Misc
*.cache
*.tmp
*.bak
