_ReSharper*/
*.tlog
*.ilk
*.pdb
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# tests/output/ is committed on purpose: the rendered documents are the record of
# what the engine produces, and a diff on them is how a change to the renderer shows
# itself. What used to be ignored here was a *second* output tree that appeared when
# the suite was run from another directory - RepositoryRoot() anchors it now, so
# there is nothing left to guard against, and ignoring the real one would quietly
# drop every new sample from a commit.

# Pulled out of the designer page to run the harness; regenerated, never edited.
designer.js

# Build leftovers from the C and Pascal samples.
*.obj
*.ppu
*.o
__pycache__/

# Fonts arrive here as archives while their licence is being established. An
# unproven one must never reach the repository by accident.
engine/Fonts/*.zip

# The font gallery is one page per family, and a family is one cut: 193 of them
# now, which is 105 MB rewritten whole on every run. It is a thing to look at
# while choosing a typeface, not a result worth a diff - test 33 still renders
# it, and still fails if a family stops drawing.
tests/output/fonts/

# [Rr]elease/ above is MSBuild's output directory, and it matches that name at any
# depth - including a release/ at the top of the repository, which is where the
# single-file builds of the two faces are written. Excluded, they would have been
# generated, committed, and simply not there.
#
# The negation has to re-include the DIRECTORY and not its contents: git stops walking
# an excluded directory, so !/release/*.html would never be reached.
!/release/
